WEBVTT

00:02.980 --> 00:04.980
<b>Spare Classroom A 
In Use</b>

00:04.000 --> 00:04.980
<b>O-Okay!</b>

00:05.750 --> 00:08.870
<b>Let's do a read-through of our script!</b>

00:08.870 --> 00:11.110
<b>Does anyone have any questions?</b>

00:13.520 --> 00:18.120
<b><i>Whoa, what's with this mood?</i></b>

00:18.410 --> 00:21.620
<b>Oh! I have a question for Fuka:</b>

00:22.210 --> 00:27.540
<b>Alucia's emotions here—is she 
more desperate? Or resolved?</b>

00:27.540 --> 00:30.820
<b>Um, it's more the latter.</b>

00:30.820 --> 00:31.740
<b>Got it!</b>

00:31.740 --> 00:34.550
<b><i>Wow, Hinami, nice assist!</i></b>

00:34.970 --> 00:36.220
<b>So...</b>

00:36.730 --> 00:37.760
<b>Like this?</b>

00:39.300 --> 00:42.860
<b>If I don't do something, you'll be killed.</b>

00:44.090 --> 00:46.520
<b>So please... let me do this.</b>

00:48.020 --> 00:49.110
<b>How's that?</b>

00:49.830 --> 00:52.110
<b>P-Perfect...</b>

00:53.190 --> 00:54.610
<b>Cool!</b>

00:54.980 --> 00:59.370
<b><i>I mean, she </i>is<i> already acting 
all the time, anyway.</i></b>

00:59.370 --> 01:04.630
<b>I hate to do this, but I have a 
student council thing after this.</b>

01:04.630 --> 01:06.710
<b>Is it okay if I slip out?</b>

01:07.020 --> 01:11.730
<b><i>A-ha! To create a pretext for 
spending less time in rehearsal,</i></b>

01:11.730 --> 01:14.920
<b><i>she starts out with a bang that'll 
make her more persuasive.</i></b>

01:15.530 --> 01:18.090
<b>From what we just saw, 
yeah, you should be fine.</b>

01:18.470 --> 01:21.150
<b>Sure—no problem.</b>

02:52.020 --> 02:56.280
<b>2nd Stage: Lv. 11 
Even fairies feel lonely when they're 
away from their spring by themselves</b>

02:52.750 --> 02:56.280
<b>Wh-Who are you? What are you doing here?</b>

02:56.570 --> 02:59.300
<b>I'm Libra, the locksmith's son.</b>

02:59.820 --> 03:01.070
<b>And this is...</b>

03:01.390 --> 03:03.240
<b>Freeze, all three of you.</b>

03:03.500 --> 03:05.450
<b>Seize that man!</b>

03:05.760 --> 03:07.450
<b>His Highness's orders!</b>

03:07.450 --> 03:08.730
<b>Resistance is useless!</b>

03:08.730 --> 03:10.210
<b>Come quietly, now!</b>

03:10.210 --> 03:14.210
<b>Having escaped execution thanks to 
Alucia's quick thinking, Libra...</b>

03:14.210 --> 03:16.130
<b>Hah! Ow ow ow...</b>

03:16.130 --> 03:19.130
<b>You can't just <i>take</i> things—that 
makes you a thief!</b>

03:19.390 --> 03:21.380
<b>Calm down, Father.</b>

03:23.660 --> 03:25.010
<b>Nice work!</b>

03:25.010 --> 03:26.390
<b>Yeah, good job.</b>

03:27.120 --> 03:29.550
<b>Our first day went off without a hitch.</b>

03:29.550 --> 03:31.850
<b>I was nervous, but I had fun.</b>

03:32.160 --> 03:34.360
<b>Yeah? Well, that's good.</b>

03:34.630 --> 03:38.610
<b>Thank you so much for all your support.</b>

03:38.860 --> 03:43.450
<b>Not at all! I'm doing this because I want to.</b>

03:43.720 --> 03:47.180
<b>But... you're so busy.</b>

03:47.180 --> 03:49.450
<b>You've got that thing with Nanami...</b>

03:50.190 --> 03:51.460
<b>The comedy skit?</b>

03:51.760 --> 03:56.680
<b>Right. That's something else you have to do.</b>

03:57.230 --> 04:00.460
<b>So, um... that's what you 
should do tomorrow.</b>

04:00.750 --> 04:03.430
<b>Huh? But what about our rehearsal here?</b>

04:03.740 --> 04:07.180
<b>I'll... I'll do my best.</b>

04:09.270 --> 04:15.640
<b>I've been thinking... You've 
changed, Hanabi's changed...</b>

04:15.640 --> 04:19.070
<b>and I'm the only one getting left behind.</b>

04:19.070 --> 04:22.950
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly</b>

04:19.520 --> 04:22.950
<b>So... it's about time I change, too.</b>

04:23.680 --> 04:25.080
<b>Oh, okay.</b>

04:25.450 --> 04:30.810
<b>Don't you think this could 
spark real change for me?</b>

04:31.230 --> 04:34.460
<b>That would be the ideal, anyway.</b>

04:34.670 --> 04:36.710
<b>Yeah. I understand.</b>

04:37.200 --> 04:39.060
<b>I'm going to go for it.</b>

04:39.710 --> 04:41.710
<b>Tomozaki</b>

04:48.400 --> 04:51.430
<b>That would be the ideal, anyway.</b>

04:52.120 --> 04:53.430
<b><i>What is it...?</i></b>

04:53.730 --> 04:56.600
<b><i>Something about that 
word—"ideal"—doesn't sit right...</i></b>

04:59.690 --> 05:01.570
<b>Spare Classroom A 
In Use</b>

05:00.130 --> 05:04.500
<b>O-Okay, let's start from the first scene.</b>

05:06.910 --> 05:10.910
<b>Top Secret</b>

05:07.220 --> 05:10.910
<b>Ta-da! I've actually finished our script!</b>

05:10.910 --> 05:12.320
<b>Wow, really?</b>

05:12.320 --> 05:15.830
<b>Now let's give our married-couple 
routine a whirl!</b>

05:15.830 --> 05:17.330
<b>Clap-clap-clap-clap!</b>

05:17.680 --> 05:19.070
<b>Hello there!</b>

05:19.070 --> 05:22.070
<b>Wait wait wait! I can't just 
jump right in like that!</b>

05:22.070 --> 05:23.360
<b>Huh? Why not?</b>

05:23.360 --> 05:25.050
<b>I haven't even seen the script!</b>

05:25.050 --> 05:27.340
<b>Even though we're friends, Brain?!</b>

05:27.740 --> 05:29.640
<b>Even though we're friends.</b>

05:29.640 --> 05:32.100
<b>See? That's what I call great flow!</b>

05:32.100 --> 05:33.350
<b>Huh?</b>

05:33.350 --> 05:35.250
<b>What we did just now!</b>

05:35.250 --> 05:36.800
<b>We were just having a normal conversation,</b>

05:36.800 --> 05:38.600
<b>but it started sounding 
like a comedy skit, right?</b>

05:38.600 --> 05:40.230
<b>Ah!</b>

05:40.480 --> 05:44.520
<b>Which makes this natural 
married-couple comedy!</b>

05:44.520 --> 05:47.240
<b>Let's get rehearsing!</b>

05:49.570 --> 05:52.490
<b><i>Hey, I know! Why don't we go to the zoo?</i></b>

05:52.810 --> 05:56.340
<b><i>I wouldn't want to be there if 
the lion escaped its enclosure.</i></b>

05:56.340 --> 05:58.880
<b><i>So I'll bring a tranquilizer gun.</i></b>

05:58.880 --> 06:01.820
<b><i>You </i>know<i> they'll confiscate it at the gates!</i></b>

06:03.660 --> 06:07.880
<b>Don't you think our usual 
conversations are funnier?</b>

06:08.210 --> 06:11.390
<b>This really feels like 
we're reading a script.</b>

06:11.680 --> 06:12.890
<b>Oh...</b>

06:13.250 --> 06:18.270
<b>The funniest comedians come across 
like they're having an impromptu chat.</b>

06:18.540 --> 06:21.920
<b>So even though memorizing 
this is part of the process,</b>

06:21.920 --> 06:25.280
<b>maybe not <i>every</i> line should 
be carved in stone.</b>

06:25.570 --> 06:28.150
<b>Yeah. But that's kind of terrifying.</b>

06:28.150 --> 06:29.710
<b>I guess...</b>

06:29.710 --> 06:34.970
<b>But you and me always have such crazy 
conversations... couldn't it work?</b>

06:34.970 --> 06:36.790
<b>Now that you mention it... maybe?</b>

06:36.790 --> 06:40.040
<b>That's right! We'll conquer the world!</b>

06:40.040 --> 06:43.040
<b>What's this "world" stuff? It's 
just the culture festival.</b>

06:43.040 --> 06:45.630
<b>See? Nice comeback!</b>

06:46.050 --> 06:47.230
<b>Sheesh...</b>

06:49.900 --> 06:56.460
<b><i>I have fun with Mimimi—and so, by 
extension, it's easy to picture us dating.</i></b>

06:57.180 --> 07:00.770
<b><i>But how is that different from being friends?</i></b>

07:02.240 --> 07:02.900
<b>Here.</b>

07:04.400 --> 07:05.900
<b>Nice work today.</b>

07:07.150 --> 07:10.400
<b>You've had a lot on your 
mind lately, huh, Brain.</b>

07:11.360 --> 07:12.690
<b>You can tell?</b>

07:12.690 --> 07:15.780
<b>Aww, c'mon! Your ol' uncle 
is always here for advice!</b>

07:15.780 --> 07:17.700
<b>My uncle, huh?</b>

07:17.950 --> 07:20.790
<b>It's not healthy to keep stuff to yourself.</b>

07:20.790 --> 07:23.870
<b>And if a girl my age is saying 
it, you <i>know</i> it's true!</b>

07:25.340 --> 07:27.840
<b>What, so you're not my uncle after all?</b>

07:28.220 --> 07:29.970
<b>Don't you worry about that.</b>

07:31.500 --> 07:33.470
<b>Um... thanks.</b>

07:33.470 --> 07:35.260
<b>F-F-For what?!</b>

07:35.590 --> 07:37.640
<b>For worrying about me.</b>

07:37.640 --> 07:40.140
<b>Oh, well, y-y-you know...</b>

07:40.400 --> 07:44.300
<b>I've actually had a lot of 
things to think about lately:</b>

07:44.800 --> 07:48.650
<b>the script for our play, Hinami...</b>

07:48.650 --> 07:50.110
<b>Aoi?</b>

07:50.110 --> 07:52.980
<b>She's playing Alucia, right?</b>

07:52.980 --> 07:55.760
<b>We asked her a lot of questions for the part,</b>

07:55.760 --> 07:58.910
<b>like, "Why do you push yourself so hard?"</b>

07:59.340 --> 08:04.360
<b>Oh, that. I've been wondering that 
myself, ever since the election.</b>

08:04.810 --> 08:07.070
<b>And how maybe she and I are the same.</b>

08:07.590 --> 08:08.800
<b>The same?</b>

08:09.120 --> 08:15.040
<b>I told you how I need to be in first 
place because I'm not special, right?</b>

08:15.500 --> 08:16.260
<b>Yeah.</b>

08:17.040 --> 08:18.700
<b>So I'm thinking...</b>

08:18.700 --> 08:23.670
<b>maybe Aoi shoots for first place 
so <i>she</i> can be special, too.</b>

08:23.670 --> 08:25.550
<b>That could be.</b>

08:27.760 --> 08:28.650
<b>Mimimi?</b>

08:29.280 --> 08:31.990
<b>If so, that worries me a little.</b>

08:32.310 --> 08:33.290
<b>How so?</b>

08:34.060 --> 08:36.240
<b>Maybe Aoi and I are the same:</b>

08:36.960 --> 08:38.540
<b>hollow.</b>

08:39.480 --> 08:42.170
<b>Hinami, hollow?</b>

08:42.790 --> 08:47.600
<b>I mean, I don't know what 
her core motivation is.</b>

08:48.270 --> 08:52.350
<b>To try that hard and still be 
empty inside... How sad is that?</b>

08:52.350 --> 08:55.510
<b>And if it's true... then she might...</b>

08:56.120 --> 08:56.890
<b>Might what?</b>

08:58.210 --> 09:02.270
<b>She might not ever come 
to me for advice. Right?</b>

09:02.660 --> 09:07.520
<b><i>It's true. I doubt Hinami would 
unload on Mimimi about herself.</i></b>

09:07.840 --> 09:10.170
<b><i>And not just Mimimi...</i></b>

09:10.170 --> 09:15.280
<b><i>I can't picture her opening 
up to anyone at all.</i></b>

09:15.280 --> 09:18.490
<b>Cast 
Libra: Takehiro Mizusawa 
Alucia: Aoi Hinami 
Kris: Hanabi Natsubayashi 
King: Shuji Nakamura 
Knight: Erika Konno</b>

09:16.000 --> 09:18.490
<b><i>How can you even </i>be<i> that strong,</i></b>

09:18.490 --> 09:21.290
<b>Aoi Hinami</b>

09:19.160 --> 09:20.720
<b><i>Aoi Hinami?</i></b>

09:23.540 --> 09:25.290
<b>Spare Classroom A 
In Use</b>

09:25.560 --> 09:28.940
<b><i>When I joined rehearsals for 
the first time in two days...</i></b>

09:29.420 --> 09:33.420
<b>Could you be more dignified 
there, please, Nakamura?</b>

09:33.690 --> 09:34.990
<b>You mean like this?</b>

09:35.510 --> 09:38.790
<b>Yikes! That's not 
dignified—that's intimidating!</b>

09:38.790 --> 09:39.460
<b>Say what?</b>

09:39.460 --> 09:42.680
<b>C'mon, a king's more like <i>this</i>!</b>

09:42.960 --> 09:45.070
<b>What's so kingly about that?</b>

09:45.070 --> 09:47.690
<b>Right? Not dignified in the slightest.</b>

09:47.690 --> 09:50.620
<b>Aw! It is too dignified!</b>

09:47.690 --> 09:50.620
<b>How long do I have to keep doing this?</b>

09:47.690 --> 09:51.690
<b>Alucia</b>

09:50.620 --> 09:51.690
<b>Want to swap?</b>

09:51.690 --> 09:54.190
<b>Cut it out already.</b>

09:52.990 --> 09:54.190
<b>Oh, thanks.</b>

09:54.190 --> 09:57.950
<b>Hey—focus! Help Fuka out here!</b>

09:59.950 --> 10:02.580
<b>Oh, sorry! Keep going.</b>

10:03.330 --> 10:05.330
<b>O-Okay, um...</b>

10:06.060 --> 10:09.080
<b>What's rehearsal been 
like these past two days?</b>

10:09.080 --> 10:14.420
<b>Oh, Kikuchi's been trying to 
really actively talk to everyone.</b>

10:14.690 --> 10:15.880
<b>To everyone?</b>

10:16.120 --> 10:19.930
<b>Yeah. Like when you were 
assigning parts earlier.</b>

10:19.930 --> 10:22.710
<b>It feels like she learned from watching you.</b>

10:22.710 --> 10:24.890
<b>Y'know, though, I hate to say this...</b>

10:25.530 --> 10:27.560
<b>She's not really used to that kind of role.</b>

10:28.480 --> 10:29.390
<b>Well... no.</b>

10:29.740 --> 10:35.340
<b>So it's like... our tires are 
spinning, and we keep losing focus.</b>

10:35.880 --> 10:38.650
<b>And Aoi hasn't been around—she's 
busy with student council work.</b>

10:44.720 --> 10:47.170
<b>Good morning, Tomozaki.</b>

10:47.170 --> 10:48.610
<b>Morning, Kikuchi.</b>

10:49.750 --> 10:51.720
<b>Could it be... finished?</b>

10:51.720 --> 10:54.880
<b>Yes. I know it took a long time, but...</b>

10:54.880 --> 10:57.170
<b>I've finished the script.</b>

10:57.430 --> 10:58.430
<b>Ooh!</b>

11:03.630 --> 11:08.770
<b><i>The script went in a different 
direction than I'd anticipated.</i></b>

11:09.120 --> 11:11.960
<b><i>After Libra and Kris took 
off on the flying dragon</i></b>

11:11.960 --> 11:14.240
<b><i>and Kris got a taste of how 
beautiful the world was,</i></b>

11:14.240 --> 11:16.530
<b><i>she began asking to venture into town.</i></b>

11:17.070 --> 11:20.860
<b><i>Libra accompanied her out of the castle.</i></b>

11:21.610 --> 11:23.450
<b><i>She didn't know how shopping worked,</i></b>

11:23.450 --> 11:25.870
<b><i>and got a real scolding from the greengrocer.</i></b>

11:25.870 --> 11:28.870
<b><i>Thus Kris came to know the real world.</i></b>

11:29.940 --> 11:31.920
<b><i>Eventually, Kris got to thinking:</i></b>

11:31.920 --> 11:33.880
<b><i>this garden she'd been cooped 
up in for all this time,</i></b>

11:34.400 --> 11:38.160
<b><i>this place she wanted to 
leave... she did nothing</i></b>

11:38.650 --> 11:41.980
<b><i>in return for clean clothes 
and delicious food,</i></b>

11:42.720 --> 11:45.390
<b><i>and she could read all the 
fairy tales she desired.</i></b>

11:45.720 --> 11:49.390
<b><i>It may have been a little too convenient.</i></b>

11:50.690 --> 11:54.400
<b>Say, Libra... am I spoiled?</b>

11:54.630 --> 11:55.520
<b>Eh?</b>

11:55.740 --> 11:59.000
<b>Being shut away in this garden,</b>

11:59.000 --> 12:01.650
<b>never having to work hard to live...</b>

12:01.920 --> 12:05.470
<b>The outside world is pretty from a distance,</b>

12:05.470 --> 12:09.160
<b>but I'll have to work hard 
if I want to be part of it.</b>

12:09.800 --> 12:13.670
<b><i>In the end, Kris sneaked out 
of the castle and went missing.</i></b>

12:14.300 --> 12:16.420
<b><i>Libra and Alucia searched 
desperately for her.</i></b>

12:16.920 --> 12:21.170
<b><i>But the castle's residents did 
nothing about the missing girl.</i></b>

12:21.720 --> 12:23.930
<b><i>Kris had finished raising the flying dragon,</i></b>

12:23.930 --> 12:27.940
<b><i>so as far as they were concerned, 
she was only baggage.</i></b>

12:29.070 --> 12:32.980
<b><i>Kris took a job at the greengrocer's.</i></b>

12:33.770 --> 12:35.790
<b><i>Despite a string of failures,</i></b>

12:35.790 --> 12:38.940
<b><i>Kris used her own skills to 
learn what life required of her,</i></b>

12:38.940 --> 12:41.230
<b><i>and decided to live in the outside world.</i></b>

12:41.820 --> 12:46.340
<b><i>Libra and Alucia celebrated her new venture.</i></b>

12:47.320 --> 12:50.140
<b><i>I sure didn't see </i>that<i> coming.</i></b>

12:50.140 --> 12:50.700
<b><i>Still...</i></b>

12:53.120 --> 12:56.500
<b><i>It's so similar to what I felt back then...</i></b>

12:57.000 --> 12:59.000
<b>Bottom-Tier Character Tomozaki S2</b>

13:01.750 --> 13:03.510
<b>I read your script.</b>

13:03.510 --> 13:05.630
<b>H-How was it?</b>

13:05.890 --> 13:10.640
<b>Um... Why was Kris... like that?</b>

13:11.400 --> 13:13.520
<b>Like what?</b>

13:14.020 --> 13:17.990
<b>She left the garden and Libra and Alucia...</b>

13:17.990 --> 13:20.950
<b>and decided to live alone 
in the village, right?</b>

13:20.950 --> 13:21.900
<b>Yes...</b>

13:21.900 --> 13:25.530
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fourth Draft</b>

13:22.400 --> 13:25.530
<b>I'm sure you put a lot of thought into this,</b>

13:25.530 --> 13:30.530
<b>but reading that actually 
made me kind of sad.</b>

13:31.390 --> 13:36.540
<b>I felt like it was negating everything 
about her life in the garden.</b>

13:40.190 --> 13:46.170
<b>One of my favorite Andi books 
is <i>The Popple on Raptor Isle</i>.</b>

13:46.170 --> 13:48.080
<b>The Popples...</b>

13:48.080 --> 13:50.930
<b>Oh, right... You mentioned that before.</b>

13:50.930 --> 13:53.620
<b>It's an incredibly positive story.</b>

13:54.130 --> 13:59.680
<b>This Popple, a blind creature, 
was living all on its lonesome</b>

13:59.680 --> 14:02.440
<b>when it left on a journey 
in search of friends.</b>

14:02.440 --> 14:07.320
<b>At first, all the other creatures 
feared it because it was different.</b>

14:07.320 --> 14:10.950
<b>But it made friends through 
the power of its words.</b>

14:10.950 --> 14:15.090
<b>And after making all these 
friends of other species,</b>

14:15.090 --> 14:17.960
<b>they all went on a voyage to see the ocean.</b>

14:18.760 --> 14:24.460
<b>After reading it, I thought this 
Popple was an ideal for the world.</b>

14:24.790 --> 14:27.470
<b>An ideal... for the world?</b>

14:27.720 --> 14:31.020
<b>It didn't even know what 
kind of creature it was,</b>

14:31.020 --> 14:34.680
<b>but it reached out to all these 
other species and made friends.</b>

14:35.280 --> 14:39.230
<b>All thanks to the power of 
language and a little effort.</b>

14:40.120 --> 14:42.960
<b>That's how it made friends.</b>

14:43.510 --> 14:46.990
<b>It reminded me of a certain two people.</b>

14:47.330 --> 14:48.740
<b>Two... You mean...</b>

14:49.090 --> 14:52.490
<b>Yes. You and Hanabi.</b>

14:54.840 --> 14:59.870
<b>I like this Popple's tale, and think 
it's a great storytelling ideal...</b>

14:59.870 --> 15:02.880
<b>an ideal for the world.</b>

15:03.510 --> 15:07.700
<b>I thought I needed to be 
more like that Popple.</b>

15:07.700 --> 15:10.840
<b>But I just kept giving up.</b>

15:10.840 --> 15:12.760
<b>Maybe it was impossible.</b>

15:13.180 --> 15:17.280
<b>But when I saw you and Hanabi, I thought:</b>

15:17.280 --> 15:21.440
<b>You're both so brilliant, 
such ideal people...</b>

15:21.440 --> 15:24.650
<b>And maybe, just maybe, I 
could be like that, too.</b>

15:24.650 --> 15:27.650
<b>So you're aiming for that ideal yourself?</b>

15:27.650 --> 15:29.880
<b>Kris is the same way.</b>

15:29.880 --> 15:34.160
<b>Working hard to change like the 
Popple did, to fit in in the world.</b>

15:34.160 --> 15:39.410
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fourth Draft</b>

15:34.500 --> 15:39.410
<b>After all, changing like that <i>is</i> ideal.</b>

15:39.970 --> 15:44.510
<b>I was fretting over who'd 
be with whom in the end.</b>

15:44.510 --> 15:49.420
<b>But this story was really 
about how Kris lives her life.</b>

15:51.260 --> 15:51.900
<b>Uh-huh.</b>

15:52.640 --> 15:53.800
<b>Got it.</b>

15:54.280 --> 15:57.230
<b>But these new parts of the script...</b>

15:57.230 --> 15:59.810
<b>Can we set them aside for now?</b>

16:00.270 --> 16:02.440
<b>Set them... aside?</b>

16:02.440 --> 16:05.910
<b>Mull over it for a while, and 
if it has to be that way,</b>

16:05.910 --> 16:07.440
<b>we'll go ahead with it as is.</b>

16:08.100 --> 16:10.170
<b>I know we don't have a lot of time, but...</b>

16:10.630 --> 16:13.700
<b>It really does feel much too sad.</b>

16:13.700 --> 16:17.700
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fourth Draft</b>

16:14.920 --> 16:16.340
<b>Understood.</b>

16:17.700 --> 16:19.700
<b>Spare Classroom A 
In Use</b>

16:19.700 --> 16:22.210
<b>Okay. Places, everyone.</b>

16:22.480 --> 16:23.710
<b>Where do I go again?</b>

16:23.710 --> 16:25.950
<b>The king's right here!</b>

16:25.950 --> 16:27.160
<b>Isn't that my spot?</b>

16:27.160 --> 16:28.960
<b><i>Is</i> it?</b>

16:29.250 --> 16:30.710
<b>I'm here, right?</b>

16:31.060 --> 16:32.590
<b>Um...</b>

16:32.590 --> 16:37.350
<b>Hey, slow down! Think about Fuka here!</b>

16:37.760 --> 16:39.200
<b>Shuji, you're here.</b>

16:39.200 --> 16:41.600
<b>Erika, you're over here, 
and Tachibana, you're here.</b>

16:42.120 --> 16:43.560
<b>Right, Fuka?</b>

16:44.130 --> 16:45.790
<b>Yes, right.</b>

16:48.170 --> 16:49.740
<b>Where am I again?</b>

16:49.740 --> 16:51.070
<b>Here, I think?</b>

16:51.070 --> 16:53.090
<b>Matsumoto, you're here,</b>

16:53.090 --> 16:54.820
<b>and Hashiguchi, you're here.</b>

16:55.850 --> 16:59.330
<b><i>Maybe it's because the school's 
perfect heroine Aoi Hinami is here,</i></b>

16:59.580 --> 17:03.080
<b><i>but Kikuchi seems to be 
mimicking how she does things.</i></b>

17:05.100 --> 17:07.580
<b>O-Okay. Let's begin.</b>

17:07.880 --> 17:09.210
<b>Why is she like that?</b>

17:09.980 --> 17:12.210
<b>Could you <i>not</i> sneak up on me?!</b>

17:13.450 --> 17:17.130
<b>Kikuchi's been thinking about a lot of stuff.</b>

17:17.640 --> 17:19.890
<b>Hmm. A lot, eh?</b>

17:20.240 --> 17:22.300
<b>Yeah, well...</b>

17:23.150 --> 17:26.390
<b>Tell me. Maybe I can help.</b>

17:27.880 --> 17:32.400
<b>She thinks she has to 
become this world ideal.</b>

17:33.260 --> 17:36.910
<b>Changing to fit in better, making friends...</b>

17:37.190 --> 17:41.410
<b>She says she has to do these 
things to fit this ideal.</b>

17:41.680 --> 17:44.050
<b>A world ideal, eh?</b>

17:44.050 --> 17:47.290
<b>I mean, sure, if she says so.</b>

17:47.690 --> 17:50.040
<b>The way she puts it feels a little loaded.</b>

17:50.320 --> 17:52.720
<b>No, I think it's a good thing.</b>

17:52.720 --> 17:54.920
<b>She's determined to change herself</b>

17:54.920 --> 17:57.580
<b>and is actively working 
toward making that happen.</b>

17:57.580 --> 18:00.930
<b>And she's doing a great job! It's impressive.</b>

18:01.950 --> 18:03.430
<b>I suppose so.</b>

18:03.720 --> 18:07.780
<b>And so is her reason for 
it: to fit this ideal.</b>

18:08.270 --> 18:12.190
<b>Pretty ironic that it's the 
opposite of <i>you</i>, though.</b>

18:12.780 --> 18:14.380
<b>The opposite?</b>

18:14.380 --> 18:18.200
<b>If you mean the directions we're moving 
in, I think they're actually the same.</b>

18:19.770 --> 18:22.880
<b>Making an effort to change so 
we fit in with everyone else.</b>

18:23.390 --> 18:25.200
<b>That's what Tama and I did.</b>

18:26.090 --> 18:29.460
<b>Ah, okay! So that's what 
it looks like to you.</b>

18:29.710 --> 18:31.210
<b>Wh-What?</b>

18:31.460 --> 18:37.220
<b>Look, Kikuchi's talking about 
the <i>world's</i> ideals, right?</b>

18:40.670 --> 18:45.100
<b>Your ideal is from your own 
perspective: "I'd like to do <i>this</i>."</b>

18:45.400 --> 18:50.350
<b>While Kikuchi's takes a bird's-eye 
view: "The world needs me like <i>this</i>."</b>

18:50.640 --> 18:52.140
<b>Totally opposite, right?</b>

18:54.010 --> 18:59.530
<b><i>I changed myself so I could enjoy 
my playthrough of this game of life.</i></b>

19:00.160 --> 19:04.540
<b><i>Tama changed herself so she 
wouldn't be making Mimimi sad.</i></b>

19:08.710 --> 19:12.170
<b><i>We both did it so we could 
be our ideal selves.</i></b>

19:12.980 --> 19:15.170
<b><i>Then why is Kikuchi doing it?</i></b>

19:17.210 --> 19:18.780
<b>Is <i>that</i> how it is?</b>

19:19.550 --> 19:22.310
<b><i>Drawing nearer to the world's ideals</i></b>

19:22.310 --> 19:28.310
<b><i>is an objective, player-oriented 
way of thinking, like Hinami's.</i></b>

19:32.780 --> 19:34.060
<b>Yes, that's right.</b>

19:34.060 --> 19:40.070
<b>I do feel like I see things from 
what you call a "player" perspective.</b>

19:42.070 --> 19:45.600
<b>But this has me thinking...</b>

19:45.600 --> 19:49.330
<b>It might actually be an author's perspective.</b>

19:49.330 --> 19:53.580
<b>An author's... like scripts and novels?</b>

19:53.580 --> 19:56.870
<b>Well, yes, those too, but more than that.</b>

19:56.870 --> 19:59.590
<b>An author of this story we call the world.</b>

19:59.980 --> 20:02.840
<b>The world's author?</b>

20:03.090 --> 20:06.800
<b>For a long time now, I haven't 
thought about what I'd like to do</b>

20:06.800 --> 20:11.450
<b>so much as how to make this world 
more beautiful, how it should be,</b>

20:11.450 --> 20:14.100
<b>what an ideal form would look like.</b>

20:14.100 --> 20:16.860
<b>A very authoresque way 
of thinking about things.</b>

20:17.610 --> 20:20.490
<b>So I'm okay with this.</b>

20:20.740 --> 20:22.990
<b>With a player perspective?</b>

20:23.530 --> 20:26.940
<b>Those are <i>your</i> words, Tomozaki.</b>

20:27.490 --> 20:33.370
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fourth Draft</b>

20:28.190 --> 20:33.370
<b>In the game world, the opposite of 
"character" may well be "player."</b>

20:33.810 --> 20:39.880
<b>But in the world of novels, I think the 
opposite of "character" is "author."</b>

20:40.160 --> 20:45.590
<b>So I'll be all right holding 
onto my author's perspective.</b>

20:48.640 --> 20:53.230
<b>I do want to take on that ideal form.</b>

20:53.230 --> 20:55.520
<b>Just like Hinami.</b>

20:55.830 --> 20:57.400
<b>Like Hinami, huh...?</b>

20:57.400 --> 20:58.400
<b>Yes.</b>

20:58.900 --> 21:02.350
<b>After all, she's a very 
ideal person, isn't she?</b>

21:03.150 --> 21:04.650
<b>Tomozaki</b>

21:06.660 --> 21:08.410
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fourth Draft 
Fuka Kikuchi</b>

21:09.170 --> 21:11.790
<b><i>The whole premise was off.</i></b>

21:12.380 --> 21:16.830
<b><i>I was playing the game of life as a player.</i></b>

21:17.120 --> 21:22.010
<b><i>Kikuchi was writing the 
story of life as an author.</i></b>

21:22.520 --> 21:26.540
<b><i>But really, she's aiming to be 
a perfect heroine like Hinami.</i></b>

21:27.480 --> 21:31.100
<b><i>Is that the path Kikuchi should be taking?</i></b>

21:31.100 --> 21:36.600
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fourth Draft 
Fuka Kikuchi</b>

21:31.690 --> 21:35.690
<b><i>Still, it's not for me to say what 
should go on inside Kikuchi's head.</i></b>

21:36.990 --> 21:39.100
<b>Inside Kikuchi's head...</b>

21:43.780 --> 21:44.610
<b>A-ha.</b>

21:44.610 --> 21:47.110
<b>The Popple on Raptor Isle 
Michael Andi 
Translated by Emiko Murata 
Read Now</b>

21:44.950 --> 21:45.780
<b>There it is.</b>

21:59.630 --> 22:02.130
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fourth Draft</b>

22:03.130 --> 22:05.010
<b><i>I read the whole thing...</i></b>

22:05.010 --> 22:11.010
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
Fourth Draft 
Fuka Kikuchi</b>

22:05.290 --> 22:09.820
<b>and found a clue that 
could give me an answer.</b>
